  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amar Subash Ghosh vs The State Of Maharashtra Thr. Pso, Ps, ... on 11 July, 2024 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Nagpur Bench : Nagpur Criminal Application (Aba) No.509 Of 2024 Amar Subash Ghosh Vs. State of Maharashtra, Through Police Station Officer, Police Station, Dhanora, District Gadchiroli ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Office Notes, Office Memoranda of Coram, appearances, Court's orders of directions and Registrar's orders ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Mr. Madhur A. Deo, Advocate for applicant. Mrs. R. V. Sharma, App for respondent/State. Coram : Urm Dated : 11/ 1.",
    "facts": "Learned submitted that the crime is registered report lodged by Suresh Posanna Torem w working as a Food Safety Officer. He re information and therefore, he conducted two-wheeler was stopped on Godalwahi-Dh (2) 14.aba.509.2024 Road which had bags that contained scented tobacco. The scented tobacco was already seized from the applicant. He submitted that considering the allegations in the FIR the offence under Section 328 is not made out.",
    "arguments": "Now, the stock is already recovered, the custodial interrogation of the present applicant is not required, in view of that he be protected by granting ad-interim anticipatory bail. 3. Learned APP strongly opposed the said application on the ground that the huge stock of scented tobacco is recovered from the present applicant, in view of that, his custodial interrogation is required. 4. After hearing the learned Counsel for the applicant and learned APP for the State, undisputedly, the issue regarding the applicability of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is pending before the Hon'ble Apex Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Now, the stock is already recovered, the custodial interrogation of the present applicant is not required, in view of that he be protected by granting ad-interim anticipatory bail. 3. Learned APP strongly opposed the said application on the ground that the huge stock of scented tobacco is recovered from the present applicant, in view of that, his custodial interrogation is required. 4. After hearing the learned Counsel for the applicant and learned APP for the State, undisputedly, the issue regarding the applicability of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is pending before the Hon'ble Apex Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
